    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0412" n="310" xml:id="pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee/661: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Delegate</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-11-18T19:00:00+01:00">November 18,
                            1933—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 18—4:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>788. For the Under Secretary. Since sending my 7871 am informed that Henderson is
                    inviting the representatives of certain great powers including ourselves with
                    the officers of the Bureau to a “tea party” tomorrow afternoon. I shall accept
                    in line with your 390.</p>
                <p>I should appreciate an expression of your views for my general guidance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
